From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 a link to another app from a bridge tab is dropped, not a crash (EP-01)

A link to a scheme that another app on the Mac handles (mailto:, zoommtg:,
slack:) reaches ExternalProtocolHandler::RunExternalProtocolDialog, which
makes Chromium's ExternalProtocolDialog. Its constructor calls
constrained_window::ShowWebModalDialogViews, and CreateWebModalDialogViews
(components/constrained_window/constrained_window_views.cc) takes the tab's
WebContentsModalDialogManager and calls manager->delegate() with no check.
A tab the host made has no such manager (tab/097 says so), so the browser
process reads through a null pointer and Darni quits, every window and
profile. Chromium lets the first such request through without a user
gesture. Security review EP-01 (security/RC-2026.1120.after-1136.md).

This is the stop-gap: when the tab (or the tab that embeds it) has no
manager, the request is dropped, and the first drop in a run writes one
warning line with the scheme only, never the address. The link then does
nothing. The real fix routes these links to the host, which asks in its
own sheet and opens the app itself; when it lands, this check stays as the
guard for any tab the host does not route.

The same unchecked read is reached by every caller of
ShowWebModalDialogViews. The ones a page can start were read at the pin:
FedCM returns when the tab has no TabInterface, and the device choosers
and PaymentRequest when no browser window holds the tab. The password
account chooser returns when the tab has no ManagePasswordsUIController.
JavaScript dialogs, HTTP auth, client certificates and WebAuthn go to the
host (tab/013, tab/056, tab/059, tab/097). The card CVC prompt is
unchecked but needs a Google Payments card. Only this one is reached by
any page with no gesture and no setup.

Type-checked with the tree's clang (out/ReArc-dev-arm64 flags, Chromium's
plugins, -fsyntax-only) against overlay 6274321b22. Not built, not run.

Touches: chrome/browser/ui/views/{external_protocol_dialog.cc, BUILD.gn}
(the target's dep on //components/web_modal). No other patch touches them.
No bridge, ABI or feature string change.

Last rebased: 2026-11-20 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.109 (overlay 6274321b22).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/views/BUILD.gn
index 3125abc..4b90b93 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/BUILD.gn
@@ -851,6 +851,7 @@ source_set("external_protocol_dialog") {
     "//components/constrained_window",
     "//components/prefs",
     "//components/url_formatter",
+    "//components/web_modal",
     "//ui/base",
     "//ui/base/mojom:ui_base_types",
     "//ui/gfx",
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/external_protocol_dialog.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/external_protocol_dialog.cc
index 6e5a662..c7bed1a 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/external_protocol_dialog.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/external_protocol_dialog.cc
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #include <utility>
 
+#include "base/logging.h"
 #include "base/strings/string_util.h"
 #include "base/types/optional_util.h"
 #include "build/build_config.h"
@@ -22,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "components/constrained_window/constrained_window_views.h"
 #include "components/prefs/pref_service.h"
 #include "components/url_formatter/elide_url.h"
+#include "components/web_modal/web_contents_modal_dialog_manager.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/weak_document_ptr.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/web_contents.h"
 #include "ui/base/l10n/l10n_util.h"
@@ -108,6 +110,19 @@ void ExternalProtocolHandler::RunExternalProtocolDialog(
     return;
   }
 
+  // ReArc: a tab the host made has no WebContentsModalDialogManager, and
+  // CreateWebModalDialogViews reads through it unchecked. Drop the request
+  // until the host routes these links itself (EP-01).
+  if (!web_modal::WebContentsModalDialogManager::FromWebContents(
+          constrained_window::GetTopLevelWebContents(web_contents))) {
+    static bool warned = false;
+    LOG_IF(WARNING, !warned)
+        << "ReArc: dropped a link to another app (" << url.scheme()
+        << ":): this tab has no dialog host";
+    warned = true;
+    return;
+  }
+
   // Windowing system takes ownership.
   new ExternalProtocolDialog(web_contents, url, program_name, initiating_origin,
                              std::move(initiator_document));
